# Issue #11: register-node.sh against AWS IoT Core for LoRaWAN, 2026-11-21, on a throwaway identity
# DevEUI ...57b2 and JoinEUI are random values made for this run; the device was deleted afterwards.
# Profiles and destination came from REGISTER_NODE_* environment variables (destination aesd_uplinks).

## 1. Dry run in a Terminal tab of the Claude desktop app (Git Bash, Windows aws.exe)
stdin is a terminal
$ scripts/register-node.sh -c -n aesd-throwaway-57b2 0BC91AFD549C57B2 E382982083C6CF5C
Node ...57b2 is not registered yet. Device profile, service profile and destination exist (LoRaWAN 1.1).
Check only (-c): nothing changed.
exit status 0

## 2. Typing keys in that tab failed: every attempt stopped before AWS was called (exit 2).
##    Cause found: Enter arrives as CR LF there, so the NwkKey prompt read an empty line;
##    after that fix, pasted keys still failed (most likely bracketed-paste markers).
##    The script now skips empty lines and strips CR and paste markers (host test cases added).

## 3. Registration and re-run, prompts answered by a pty harness in WSL with random keys
##    (Python secrets.token_hex(16), never printed or saved), aws.exe through a path-converting wrapper
